[38;5;252m[1m## Two findings worth calling out[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mThe [38;5;10mj[0m overflow regime is reachable, and it agrees.[22m [38;5;10mj += 2[0m leaves [38;5;10mint[0m range at [38;5;10mi = 2³⁰[0m. I initially wrote this off as untestable, but a throughput probe showed ~92 s per library, so [38;5;10mheavy::cfg_c11_j_signed_overflow[0m runs it for real at [38;5;10mx = 2³⁰ + 4096[0m: 21,955,747,671 bytes streamed and FNV-hashed per side, identical hashes. To prove the boundary was actually crossed rather than both sides just agreeing on a shorter run, the byte count is checked against a closed-form two's-complement-wrapping model (matches exactly) and against a non-wrapping model (21,955,743,575 — excluded). So gcc's codegen wraps, [38;5;10mwrapping_add(2)[0m reproduces it, and 4096 lines really do carry [38;5;10mj < 0[0m starting at [38;5;10m-2147483648[0m.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mTwo harness bugs, no translation bugs.[22m Six tests failed on the first run; both causes were in my test code:[0m[0m
- fd 1 is process-global, and libtest writes its own [38;5;10mtest X ... ok[0m progress lines to it from the main thread, landing inside worker-thread captures. Fixed with [38;5;10m.cargo/config.toml[0m forcing [38;5;10mRUST_TEST_THREADS=1[0m, plus a contamination detector so this reports as [38;5;10mCAPTURE CONTAMINATED[0m rather than masquerading as a divergence.[0m[0m
- The forked-child prefix reader used [38;5;10m_exit[0m, which skips libc's atexit flush and silently dropped the last partial stdout buffer (102400 vs 103335 bytes). Caught only by [38;5;10mcfg_c10_prefix_machinery_selfcheck[0m, which exists to stop C10 passing vacuously.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The Rust source needed no changes — it already called the same libc [38;5;10mprintf[0m (so buffering and byte output are identical by construction) and already used [38;5;10mwrapping_add[0m. [38;5;10mc_src/[0m is unmodified apart from the [38;5;10mbuild/[0m directory the instructions asked for; I removed my scratch probe directory.[0m[0m
